  "headline": "Three findings: (1) Complex-S3 \u03b1_p is NOT cluster-constant (max|z|=3.3 across p \u2208 {5,7,11,13}; R18h-era cluster hypothesis rejected). (2) D4 quartic shows NO convergence to naive Cohen-Martinet (\u03b1 \u2248 -0.1 with poor R\u00b2 0.46-0.59; empirical stays persistently off). (3) S4 complex quartic converges at a NEW universal rate \u03b1 \u2248 0.048 (cluster-constant at 2\u03c3 across p \u2208 {5,7,11,13}), far slower than DH 1/6 but internally consistent \u2014 Tier-2 F-anchor candidate.",
  "interpretation": {
    "complex_s3_universality": {
      "verdict": "REJECTED at 2\u03c3 and 3\u03c3",
      "weighted_mean": 0.2164,
      "max_abs_z": 3.323,
      "implication": "Complex-S3 \u03b1_p varies with p in a way not captured by a single constant. The R18h provisional cluster claim was based on 4 primes with overlapping SEs; the universality test now rejects it. The structure may still be prime-independent at a higher-moment level (e.g., log(p) scaling), but as a simple constant \u2014 no."
    },
    "d4_quartic_nonconvergence": {
      "verdict": "\u03b1 \u2248 -0.1 with R\u00b2 \u2248 0.5, cluster-constant across primes",
      "interpretation": "The naive Cohen-Martinet unit-rank formula (1 - \u220f_{k=u+1}^\u221e (1-p^-k)) does NOT fit D4 empirical Prob(p|h). D4 has non-trivial G-module structure \u2014 the intermediate quadratic subfield contributes a 2-part modification to the class-group distribution that the naive CM ignores. For odd primes p \u2209 {2, ...}, the refined Cohen-Martinet formula for D4 should incorporate the D4-module decomposition of Cl(K) \u2297 Z_p. Literature: Bartel-Lenstra 2020 gives the corrected heuristic for D4; not encoded here. Opens track: replace CM with Bartel-Lenstra D4 and re-fit.",
      "cluster_constancy_despite_wrong_formula": "Even with wrong prediction, \u03b1 is cluster-constant across primes \u2014 suggests the bias pattern is UNIVERSAL in p (affecting all primes equally), just offset. Consistent with a systematic rate-exponent mismatch, not per-prime noise."
    },
    "s4_complex_new_universal_rate": {
      "verdict": "\u03b1_S4_complex \u2248 0.048 \u00b1 0.004, cluster-constant at 2\u03c3",
      "per_prime": {
        "5": 0.0587,
        "7": 0.0515,
        "11": 0.0439,
        "13": 0.0429
      },
      "interpretation": "S4 complex quartic converges to the Cohen-Martinet prediction at a rate \u03b1 \u2248 0.048 \u2014 far slower than DH 1/6 (0.167) but internally CONSISTENT across primes. This is a TIER-2 F-anchor candidate: \"S4 complex quartic has a universal convergence rate \u2248 0.048.\" Mechanism: S4 has |G|=24, so the admissible |disc| grows rapidly with conductor; at the LMFDB-cutoff regime (|disc| \u2264 10^7 = bucket 6), we are deep in the small-|disc| regime of S4, far from asymptote. The slow rate is consistent with this positioning. A FULL S4 enumeration (beyond LMFDB cutoff) would test whether \u03b1 \u2248 0.048 reflects finite-|disc| or is a true asymptotic S4 rate.",
      "s4_real_insufficient_data": "S4 real quartic had n < 500 in every adequate bucket (cutoff at bucket 6 per R18i; small-|disc| S4 real is very rare). Cannot fit."
    },
    "dh_1_6_scope_narrowed": {
      "holds_for": [
        "Imaginary quadratic Prob(p=3 | h)",
        "Real quadratic Prob(p=3 | h)",
        "Scholz 3/2 ratio convergence",
        "Real S3 cubic Prob(p \u2265 5 | h) (within envelope)"
      ],
      "does_not_hold_for": [
        "Complex S3 cubic Prob(p \u2265 5 | h) \u2014 faster (\u03b1 \u2248 0.22)",
        "D4 quartic Prob(p \u2265 5 | h) \u2014 no convergence to naive CM",
        "S4 complex quartic Prob(p \u2265 5 | h) \u2014 much slower (\u03b1 \u2248 0.048)"
      ],
      "insight": "DH 1/6 is NOT a universal Cohen-Lenstra rate. It is specifically a QUADRATIC 3-torsion rate. For higher-degree non-abelian extensions, the rate depends on Galois group structure, signature, and the specific prime. The \"1/6\" exponent in Davenport-Heilbronn is tied to the error term in cubic field counting \u2014 which applies to quadratic class groups because of Scholz reflection, but does NOT automatically generalize to cubic/quartic class groups themselves."
    },
    "opens_tracks": [
      "R18k candidate: Bartel-Lenstra refined Cohen-Martinet for D4; re-fit \u03b1",
      "R18l candidate: extend S4 data beyond LMFDB cutoff via a new enumeration (out of scope here)",
      "R18m candidate: complex-S3 \u03b1_p functional form \u2014 does \u03b1_{complex_S3}(p) = f(p) for some simple f?",
      "R18n candidate: test Cohen-Martinet for other degree-6 strata (6T3, 6T11, etc.) to map DH-universality limits"
    ]
  }
